You are tasked with creating a Java program that utilizes reflection to analyze and manipulate classes and their members. In this problem, you will be working with a class named `PacketPlayOut` and its subclasses. The `PacketPlayOut` class is an abstract class that serves as a base for various packet classes used in a networking application.

Your task is to implement a method that analyzes the `PacketPlayOut` class and its subclasses to gather information about their constructors, fields, and methods. You will then organize and present this information in a structured format.

Your program should perform the following tasks:
1. Retrieve the names and parameter types of all constructors in the `PacketPlayOut` class and its subclasses.
2. Collect the names and types of all fields in the `PacketPlayOut` class and its subclasses, along with their access modifiers.
3. Gather the names, parameter types, and return types of all methods in the `PacketPlayOut` class and its subclasses, along with their access modifiers.

Your program should output the collected information in a clear and organized manner, allowing for easy analysis of the class structure and its members.

### Solution:
```java
import java.lang.reflect.Constructor;
import java.lang.reflect.Field;
import java.lang.reflect.Method;
import java.lang.reflect.Modifier;
import java.util.ArrayList;
import java.util.HashMap;
import java.util.List;
import java.util.Map;

public class PacketAnalyzer {

    public static void analyzePacketClass(Class<?> packetClass) {
        System.out.println("Analyzing class: " + packetClass.getSimpleName());
        System.out.println("Constructors:");
        Constructor<?>[] constructors = packetClass.getDeclaredConstructors();
        for (Constructor<?> constructor : constructors) {
            System.out.println(constructor.getName() + " - Parameters: " + getParameterTypes(constructor));
        }
        System.out.println("Fields:");
        Field[] fields = packetClass.getDeclaredFields();
        for (Field field : fields) {
            System.out.println(getFieldInfo(field));
        }
        System.out.println("Methods:");
        Method[] methods = packetClass.getDeclaredMethods();
        for (Method method : methods) {
            System.out.println(getMethodInfo(method));
        }
    }

    private static String getParameterTypes(Constructor<?> constructor) {
        Class<?>[] parameterTypes = constructor.getParameterTypes();
        List<String> parameterTypeNames = new ArrayList<>();
        for (Class<?> parameterType : parameterTypes) {
            parameterTypeNames.add(parameterType.getSimpleName());
        }
        return String.join(", ", parameterTypeNames);
    }

    private static String getFieldInfo(Field field) {
        String modifiers = Modifier.toString(field.getModifiers());
        String typeName = field.getType().getSimpleName();
        return modifiers + " " + typeName + " " + field.getName();
    }

    private static String getMethodInfo(Method method) {
        String modifiers = Modifier.toString(method.getModifiers());
        String returnType = method.getReturnType().getSimpleName();
        String methodName = method.getName();
        Class<?>[] parameterTypes = method.getParameterTypes();
        List<String> parameterTypeNames = new ArrayList<>();
        for (Class<?> parameterType : parameterTypes) {
            parameterTypeNames.add(parameterType.getSimpleName());
        }
        return modifiers + " " + returnType + " " + methodName + " - Parameters: " + String.join(", ", parameterTypeNames);
    }

    public static void main(String[] args) {
        analyzePacketClass(PacketPlayOut.class);
    }
}
```

