### Solution:
```csharp
public class Location
{
    public int Start { get; set; }
}

public class Region
{
    public int Start { get; set; }
    public int End { get; set; }
}

public enum RegionPlace
{
    inside,
    outside,
    overlapping
}

public class RegionUtility
{
    public static RegionPlace DetermineRegionPlace(Location currentLocation, Region region)
    {
        if (currentLocation.Start >= region.Start && currentLocation.Start <= region.End)
        {
            return RegionPlace.inside;
        }
        else if (currentLocation.Start < region.Start)
        {
            if (currentLocation.Start < region.Start && currentLocation.Start < region.End)
            {
                return RegionPlace.overlapping;
            }
            else
            {
                return RegionPlace.outside;
            }
        }
        else
        {
            return RegionPlace.outside;
        }
    }
}
```

In the `DetermineRegionPlace` function, we first check if the `currentLocation.Start` is within the `region.Start` and `region.End`. If it is, we return `RegionPlace.inside`. If not, we check if the `currentLocation.Start` is less than `region.Start`. If it is, we further check if it is also less than `region.End` to determine if it's overlapping, otherwise, we return `RegionPlace.outside`. If none of the above conditions are met, we return `RegionPlace.outside`.

