{
    public static bool TryPercentDecodeUtf8(Span<byte> buffer, ref int readHead, ref int writeHead)
    {
        // Your implementation here
    }
}
```

### Solution:
```csharp
using System;

public class UrlDecoder
{
    public static bool TryPercentDecodeUtf8(Span<byte> buffer, ref int readHead, ref int writeHead)
    {
        while (readHead < buffer.Length && buffer[readHead] == (byte)'%')
        {
            if (readHead + 2 < buffer.Length)
            {
                if (TryHexDecode(buffer.Slice(readHead + 1, 2), out byte decodedByte))
                {
                    buffer[writeHead++] = decodedByte;
                    readHead += 3;
                }
                else
                {
                    return false; // Invalid percent-encoded sequence
                }
            }
            else
            {
                return false; // Incomplete percent-encoded sequence
            }
        }

        while (readHead < buffer.Length)
        {
            buffer[writeHead++] = buffer[readHead++];
        }

        return true;
    }

    private static bool TryHexDecode(Span<byte> hexBytes, out byte decodedByte)
    {
        if (byte.TryParse(Encoding.UTF8.GetString(hexBytes), System.Globalization.NumberStyles.HexNumber, null, out decodedByte))
        {
            return true;
        }
        else
        {
            decodedByte = 0;
            return false;
        }
    }
}
```

In the solution, the `TryPercentDecodeUtf8` function iterates through the buffer, checking for the presence of URL-encoded sequences. If a valid sequence is found, it decodes the hexadecimal representation into the corresponding UTF-8 byte and writes it to the buffer at the `writeHead` position. The `readHead` and `writeHead` are appropriately updated during the decoding process. The function returns `true` if the decoding is successful and `false` if any error occurs. The `TryHexDecode` function is used to decode the hexadecimal representation into a byte.

