The PDF file contains the following format for each product:
- Product Name: [name]
- Price: [price]
- Quantity: [quantity]

You should assume that the PDF file is well-formatted and contains the product information in the specified format.

Write a program that accomplishes the following:
1. Read the provided PDF file using the Spire.Pdf library.
2. Extract the product information (name, price, quantity) from the PDF.
3. Calculate the total value of the products by multiplying the price with the quantity for each product.
4. Display the total value of the products.

### Solution:
```csharp
using Spire.Pdf;
using System;
using System.Linq;

namespace PDFProductExtractor
{
    class Program
    {
        static void Main(string[] args)
        {
            string pdfFilePath = "path_to_your_pdf_file.pdf"; // Replace with the actual path to the PDF file

            // Load the PDF document
            PdfDocument pdf = new PdfDocument();
            pdf.LoadFromFile(pdfFilePath);

            // Extract text from the PDF
            string pdfText = string.Join(" ", pdf.Pages.Select(page => page.ExtractText()));

            // Split the text into lines
            string[] lines = pdfText.Split(new[] { "\r\n", "\r", "\n" }, StringSplitOptions.RemoveEmptyEntries);

            // Initialize total value
            decimal totalValue = 0;

            // Process each line to extract product information and calculate total value
            foreach (string line in lines)
            {
                if (line.StartsWith("Product Name:"))
                {
                    string productName = line.Replace("Product Name:", "").Trim();
                    string priceLine = lines.FirstOrDefault(l => l.Contains("Price:"));
                    string quantityLine = lines.FirstOrDefault(l => l.Contains("Quantity:"));

                    if (priceLine != null && quantityLine != null)
                    {
                        decimal price = decimal.Parse(priceLine.Replace("Price:", "").Trim());
                        int quantity = int.Parse(quantityLine.Replace("Quantity:", "").Trim());

                        totalValue += price * quantity;
                    }
                }
            }

            // Display the total value of the products
            Console.WriteLine("Total value of the products: " + totalValue);

            // Dispose the PDF document
            pdf.Close();
        }
    }
}
```

In this solution, we use the Spire.Pdf library to load the PDF file and extract its text content. We then process the text to identify product information, calculate the total value of the products, and display the result.

