### Problem:
You are given a string containing a sequence of characters. Your task is to implement a program that sorts the characters in the string in a specific manner. The sorting algorithm should compare each character with the next one in the string. If the ASCII value of the current character is higher than the ASCII value of the next character, the two characters should be swapped. After sorting, the program should print the resulting string.

For example, given the input string "cbad", the program should output "abcd" after sorting the characters based on their ASCII values.

Write a program that takes a string as input, sorts the characters based on the specified criteria, and prints the resulting string.

### Solution:
```csharp
using System;

class Program
{
    static void Main()
    {
        string userInput = "cbad"; // Replace with any input string
        char temp;

        for (int j = 0; j < userInput.Length - 1; j++)
        {
            for (int i = 0; i < userInput.Length - 1; i++)
            {
                if (userInput[i] > userInput[i + 1])
                {
                    // Switch the items if the value is higher than the next
                    temp = userInput[i + 1];
                    userInput = userInput.Remove(i + 1, 1).Insert(i + 1, userInput[i].ToString());
                    userInput = userInput.Remove(i, 1).Insert(i, temp.ToString());
                }
            }
        }

        // Print the result
        foreach (char c in userInput)
        {
            Console.Write(c);
        }
    }
}
```

This program takes the input string "cbad", sorts the characters based on their ASCII values, and prints the resulting string "abcd".

