```

### Solution:
```java
public class ReverseWords {
    public static String reverseWords(String input) {
        String[] words = input.split("\\s+"); // Split the input string into an array of words
        StringBuilder reversed = new StringBuilder();

        for (int i = words.length - 1; i >= 0; i--) {
            reversed.append(words[i]); // Append each word in reverse order
            if (i > 0) {
                reversed.append(" "); // Add a space between words, except for the last word
            }
        }

        return reversed.toString();
    }

    public static void main(String[] args) {
        String input = "Hello world, how are you?";
        System.out.println(reverseWords(input)); // Output: "you? are how world, Hello"
    }
}
```

The `reverseWords` function first splits the input string into an array of words using the regular expression "\\s+" to match one or more whitespace characters. It then iterates through the array of words in reverse order, appending each word to a `StringBuilder` with a space in between. Finally, it returns the reversed string obtained from the `StringBuilder`.

