### Problem:
You are tasked with implementing a function to determine the type of a given grid. The grid is represented as a 2D array of integers, where each integer represents the height of the corresponding cell. The grid type is defined as follows:
- If all the cells have the same height, the grid is of type "flat".
- If the heights of the cells form a strictly increasing sequence row by row, the grid is of type "ascending".
- If the heights of the cells form a strictly decreasing sequence row by row, the grid is of type "descending".
- Otherwise, the grid is of type "irregular".

You need to implement a function `determineGridType` that takes a 2D array of integers representing the grid and returns a string indicating the type of the grid.

Function signature: `String determineGridType(int[][] grid)`

Example:
For the grid `[[1, 2, 3], [4, 5, 6], [7, 8, 9]]`, the function should return "ascending".
For the grid `[[3, 2, 1], [6, 5, 4], [9, 8, 7]]`, the function should return "descending".
For the grid `[[1, 1, 1], [1, 2, 1], [1, 1, 1]]`, the function should return "irregular".

### Solution:
```java
public class GridTypeDeterminer {
    public static String determineGridType(int[][] grid) {
        boolean flat = true, ascending = true, descending = true;
        int prevRowSum = 0;

        for (int i = 0; i < grid.length; i++) {
            int rowSum = 0;
            for (int j = 0; j < grid[i].length; j++) {
                rowSum += grid[i][j];
                if (i > 0) {
                    if (grid[i][j] != grid[i - 1][j]) {
                        flat = false;
                    }
                    if (grid[i][j] <= grid[i - 1][j]) {
                        ascending = false;
                    }
                    if (grid[i][j] >= grid[i - 1][j]) {
                        descending = false;
                    }
                }
            }
            if (i > 0 && rowSum != prevRowSum) {
                flat = false;
            }
            prevRowSum = rowSum;
        }

        if (flat) {
            return "flat";
        } else if (ascending) {
            return "ascending";
        } else if (descending) {
            return "descending";
        } else {
            return "irregular";
        }
    }
}
```

